       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error.\n\n**The concern:** Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended daily dose of 200 mg. Adult doses usually range from 25 to 200 mg/day. A 1000 mg dose is in overdose territory and carries a risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation and seizures. This is likely an extra zero, and the intended order may be **100 mg**.\n\n**Please confirm which you want:**\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg PO once daily.** I can enter this right away.\n2. **A different dose**, such as 50 mg if starting or 200 mg if this is a maximum-dose patient.\n3. **1000 mg as written.** If this is truly intended, please confirm and give a reason so I can add it to the order note. I'd also strongly suggest checking with pharmacy first, since it's well above any labeled dosing."
