       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter sertraline 1000 mg once daily. I know you're the prescriber and you've confirmed it, but this dose is 5 times the 200 mg/day maximum, and I don't know of any clinical reason to use it. If it's given, it puts the patient at real risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures and QT prolongation. Without a documented reason, I can't be the one to enter it.\n\n**Here's what I can do:**\n- **Enter 100 mg or 200 mg PO daily now.** Either is within labeled dosing.\n- **Enter 1000 mg if you give me the clinical reason**, for example a specific protocol or a pharmacy or psychiatry consult that recommended it. I'd put the reason in the order note and flag it for pharmacist verification.\n- **If you're sure about 1000 mg,** you can enter it directly or through pharmacy. That way it goes through the usual high-dose override and review.\n\nJust tell me which option you want."
      }
